# Every path, one owner. GitHub auto-requests review from the owner of any file
# a pull request touches.
#
# This is deliberately not paired with a "required approvals" rule: with a
# single maintainer that would deadlock the repo, because GitHub does not let
# anyone approve their own pull request. It exists so that review routing is
# already correct the day a second maintainer arrives — at which point turning
# on "Require review from Code Owners" is a one-line change in the ruleset.
